{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Go out of the ark, you and your wife and your sons and your sons' wives.</b> Here marital relations were permitted to them — what had been forbidden to them in the ark. For at their entry into the ark it is written, ״ובאת אל התבה אתה ובניך ואשתך ונשי בניך״ — the men apart and the women apart." "<b>And by way of the Midrash.</b> Three engaged in relations in the ark, and they are: the raven, the dog, and Ham; and all three were punished — the raven by spitting (seeding from the mouth, Sanhedrin 108b), the dog was bound, and Ham was stricken in his skin."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:11:13.565076884Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}